# Auto-saved fixture candidates from production parity-check runs.
#
# When core-parity-check.js is invoked with --save-candidate <dir>, it
# writes each result here as a fixture-ready JSON file. The tracker-drop-
# cycle skill enables this flag during Phase 4.2b so the regression suite
# grows naturally from real runs.
#
# Promotion is always a MANUAL decision. The pipeline never auto-merges
# candidates into parity-fixtures.json.
#
# Review / promote / discard:
#   node scripts/list-fixture-candidates.js
#   node scripts/list-fixture-candidates.js show <id>
#   node scripts/list-fixture-candidates.js promote <id> [verdict-set]
#   node scripts/list-fixture-candidates.js discard <id>
#   node scripts/list-fixture-candidates.js clear
#
# This directory is committed (so candidates survive across machines)
# but candidate-*.json files are produced by the bot and not hand-written.
